module

public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.DividedPowers.Ring

/-!
# Compatible divided power structures

Let `(A, I, γ)` and `(B, J, δ)` be divided power rings and let `f : A → B` be a ring
homomorphism. The two divided power structures are *compatible* along `f` when they both
extend to a single divided power structure on the ideal `J + f(I)B`: that is, when there is
a divided power structure `ε` on `J + f(I)B` such that `f` is a divided power map from
`(A, I, γ)` to `(J + f(I)B, ε)` and the identity of `B` is a divided power map from
`(B, J, δ)` to `(J + f(I)B, ε)`.

Compatibility is the hypothesis under which the divided powers of the base propagate to the
divided power envelopes computed over `B`; it is strictly weaker than asking that `f` itself
be a divided power map `(A, I, γ) → (B, J, δ)`, since the common extension lives on the
larger ideal `J + f(I)B`.

## Main definitions

* `Crystalline.DividedPowerRing.IsCompatible` — compatibility of the divided power structures
  of `A` and `B` along a ring homomorphism `A → B`.

## Implementation notes

The ideal generated by the image of the source ideal is `Ideal.map f`. The two required
homomorphisms of divided power rings are expressed using Mathlib's
`DividedPowers.IsDPMorphism`; the second has underlying ring map the identity of the target
ring. This predicate is an abbreviation so clients can use the morphism conditions directly.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07HK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07HK)
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u v

namespace Crystalline

/-- Compatibility of the divided power structures of `A` and `B` along `f`: both structures
extend to one on the sum of the distinguished ideal of `B` and the extension of that of `A`. -/
@[stacks 07HK] public abbrev DividedPowerRing.IsCompatible
    (A : _root_.DividedPowerRing.{u}) (B : _root_.DividedPowerRing.{v})
    (f : A.carrier →+* B.carrier) : Prop :=
  ∃ ε : DividedPowers (B.ideal + A.ideal.map f), DividedPowers.IsDPMorphism A.dividedPowers ε f ∧
    DividedPowers.IsDPMorphism B.dividedPowers ε (RingHom.id B.carrier)

end Crystalline

end
